## 26. FRONTEND EXCELLENCE STANDARD (READ BEFORE BUILDING ANY UI)

Sections 26 to 35 define the professional frontend and visual-design standard of the website. When any earlier section is less specific about a visual or layout detail, these sections take precedence.

The target quality bar: the website must look and behave like a funded, professionally designed healthcare product (the level of a polished SaaS or a leading clinic-booking platform), not like a generated template.

Non-negotiable principles:

1. Consistency: the same element looks, behaves, and sits in the same place on every page and every role.
2. Hierarchy: on every screen there is exactly one primary action, one clear page title, and a clear reading order.
3. Alignment: everything snaps to the spacing grid; nothing is "almost aligned".
4. Completeness: every data-driven view has loading, empty, error, and populated states, all designed.
5. Restraint: few colors, few font sizes, few shadows, few animations, applied with discipline.
6. Accessibility is part of the design, not an afterthought.

## 27. DESIGN TOKENS AND FOUNDATIONS

Extend src/theme/tokens.css with the following systems. No component may use a raw pixel, color, or duration that is not a token.

### Spacing scale (4px base)

--space-1: 4px; --space-2: 8px; --space-3: 12px; --space-4: 16px; --space-5: 20px; --space-6: 24px; --space-8: 32px; --space-10: 40px; --space-12: 48px; --space-16: 64px; --space-20: 80px.

Rules:
- Padding inside cards: 16px mobile, 20px tablet, 24px desktop.
- Gap between cards in a grid: 16px mobile, 24px desktop.
- Vertical gap between page sections: 32px mobile, 40px desktop.
- Page horizontal padding: 16px mobile, 24px tablet, 32px desktop.

### Color tints

Only tints and shades of the three brand colors, the two semantic colors, and the neutrals may be derived (for hover, pressed, subtle backgrounds, and borders). Do not introduce new hues. Define them as tokens, for example:

- --color-teal-hover, --color-teal-pressed, --color-teal-subtle (very light teal for selected rows and active nav items).
- --color-orange-hover, --color-orange-pressed, --color-orange-subtle (very light orange for highlighted callouts).
- --color-green-subtle and --color-red-subtle (very light backgrounds for status badges and alerts, always paired with the full-strength color for text/icon and a visible label).

### Orange contrast rule (important)

Neon orange (#FF5533) on white does not meet WCAG AA for small text. Therefore:
- Orange is used for: primary call-to-action fills, active indicators, focus rings, key icons at 24px or larger, progress fills, badges' accent dots, and large numbers (24px or larger).
- White text on an orange fill is allowed only for labels that are bold and at least 18.7px (WCAG large text). Standard-size buttons use a dark teal fill with white text.
- Never use orange for small body text, small links, or thin 1px strokes on white.
- Orange text on white is allowed only at 24px or larger.

### Typography

Font: Cairo (bundled locally). Weights used: 400, 600, 700 only.

Type scale (use fluid sizes with clamp where noted):
- Display: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px) / line-height 1.3 / weight 700 (welcome page only).
- H1: clamp(24px, 3vw, 30px) / 1.4 / 700.
- H2: 22px / 1.4 / 700.
- H3: 18px / 1.5 / 600.
- Body: 16px / 1.75 / 400.
- Body strong: 16px / 1.75 / 600.
- Small: 14px / 1.6 / 400.
- Caption: 13px / 1.5 / 400 (never below 13px).

Arabic typography rules:
- Arabic needs generous line-height (1.6 to 1.8 for body text).
- No letter-spacing on Arabic text. No italics. No uppercase transforms.
- Use text-wrap: balance on headings and text-wrap: pretty on paragraphs.
- Use bdi or dir="ltr" for embedded Latin fragments, phone numbers, emails, and English drug names so punctuation does not jump around in RTL.
- Use tabular numbers (font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums) for prices, queue numbers, times, and table columns.

### Numbers, dates, currency, and plurals

- Digits: Western digits (0 to 9) by default for phone numbers, booking numbers, times, and prices. Provide a formatNumber utility so Arabic-Indic digits can be enabled later from one place.
- Dates: Intl.DateTimeFormat with the ar-EG locale and Gregorian calendar, for example "الخميس، 5 نوفمبر 2026".
- Time: 12-hour format with Arabic markers (ص and م).
- Currency: Egyptian pounds via Intl.NumberFormat, shown as "350 ج.م".
- Arabic plural rules via Intl.PluralRules (for example: مريض واحد، مريضان، 3 مرضى، 11 مريضًا). Build a small pluralize helper; never write "مريض(ين)".
- Relative time in Arabic (for example "منذ 5 دقائق") via Intl.RelativeTimeFormat.

### Radius, borders, and elevation

- Radius: 10px (inputs, chips), 12px (buttons, small cards), 16px (cards, modals). Avatars are circles.
- Borders: 1px solid var(--color-border) is the default separator. Prefer borders to shadows.
- Elevation (maximum three levels): none (default cards, border only), sm (dropdowns, sticky bars), md (modals and bottom sheets). Shadows are soft and low-opacity, tinted with dark teal rather than pure black.

### Iconography

- lucide-react only. Stroke width 1.75. Sizes: 16 (inline in text), 20 (buttons and inputs), 24 (navigation and cards), 32 and above (empty states and onboarding).
- Icons that imply direction (chevrons, arrows, "back", "next", progress arrows) must be mirrored in RTL. Icons that do not imply direction (clock, check, calendar, phone, bell, search, map pin) must NOT be mirrored.
- Icon plus label is preferred for navigation; icon-only buttons must have an accessible name and a tooltip.
- Each domain concept uses the same icon everywhere (for example: calendar for appointments, users for the queue, stethoscope for doctors, pill for medicines, file-text for records, map-pin for locations).

### Motion

- Durations: 120ms (hover and press), 200ms (dropdowns, tabs), 280ms (modals, sheets, page fades). Easing: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1) for entering, ease-in for leaving.
- Allowed motion: opacity, small translate (maximum 8px), and scale 0.98 to 1. No bouncing, no parallax, no auto-playing animation.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion by disabling all non-essential motion.

### Z-index scale

--z-base: 0; --z-sticky: 100; --z-dropdown: 200; --z-drawer: 300; --z-modal: 400; --z-toast: 500; --z-demo-banner: 600. No arbitrary z-index values anywhere.

## 28. COMPONENT LIBRARY SPECIFICATION

Build a small internal component library in src/components/common and src/components/forms. Every component is fully typed, accessible, and supports every state listed below: default, hover, focus-visible, active/pressed, disabled, loading, error (where relevant).

### Buttons

- Variants: primary (orange fill, only one per view), secondary (dark teal fill), outline (teal border), ghost (text only), danger (red, for destructive actions only), success-confirm (green, only for confirm-complete actions such as "Finish Examination").
- Sizes: sm 40px, md 48px (default), lg 56px (booking confirmation and key mobile CTAs). Minimum touch target 44px.
- Icon placement: icon on the leading side of the label (right side in RTL). Loading state replaces the icon with a spinner and keeps the button width stable.
- Full-width on mobile when it is the primary action of a form.

### Form controls

- Labels always sit above the field (never placeholder-only labels). Required fields are marked with an Arabic "(مطلوب)" text, not only an asterisk.
- Input height 48px, radius 10px, 1px border, focus shows a 2px orange ring with offset. Font size at least 16px so mobile browsers do not zoom.
- Helper text below the field in secondary color; error text below the field in red with an alert icon. Errors are linked with aria-describedby and the field uses aria-invalid.
- Validation happens on blur and on submit (not on every keystroke), with a short error summary at the top of long forms that links to the first invalid field.
- Provide: TextInput, PhoneInput (Egyptian format with LTR display), TextArea (with character counter), Select, Combobox (searchable), Checkbox, RadioGroup, Switch, SegmentedControl, DatePicker, TimeSlotPicker, SearchInput (with clear button and keyboard shortcut hint on desktop), StarRatingInput, FileDropzone (simulated, stores metadata only).
- DatePicker: custom lightweight calendar with Arabic month and weekday names, week starting on Saturday, disabled dates clearly marked, today highlighted, selected day in dark teal, available days marked with a small orange dot. Fully keyboard operable.
- TimeSlotPicker: responsive grid of selectable chips, grouped as "صباحًا" and "مساءً", unavailable slots visibly disabled with a strikethrough style and aria-disabled, selected slot filled in dark teal with a check icon.

### Display components

- Card (flat, bordered, optional interactive variant with hover border and subtle teal background).
- StatusBadge: icon plus Arabic label plus tinted background. Mapping: Booked (teal), Waiting (orange-subtle with clock icon), Arrived (teal with user-check), In Examination (teal solid with activity icon), Completed (green with check), No Show (neutral-dark with user-x), Cancelled (red with x-circle). Color is never the only signal.
- Avatar: circle with initials, background chosen deterministically from brand tints, sizes 32, 40, 56, 96.
- Tabs (underline style, scrollable on mobile with fade edges), SegmentedControl, Breadcrumbs (mirrored separators), Accordion, Timeline (vertical, line on the start side), Stepper (horizontal on desktop, compact "الخطوة 2 من 5" with a progress bar on mobile), Rating (read-only stars with numeric value and review count), ProgressBar and ProgressRing (SVG), Tooltip, DropdownMenu, Pagination, Skeleton, EmptyState, ErrorState, InlineAlert (info, success, warning, error), Toast, ConfirmDialog, BottomSheet.
- Table: sticky header, zebra not required, row hover with subtle teal, density options (comfortable and compact), sortable columns with aria-sort, row actions in a trailing overflow menu, and automatic conversion to stacked cards below 768px.

### Overlays

- Modal: centered on desktop (max width 560px, radius 16px), bottom sheet on mobile (full width, top radius 16px, drag handle, safe-area padding). Focus trap, Escape to close, backdrop click closes only non-destructive modals, focus returns to the trigger.
- ConfirmDialog for destructive actions: red confirm button on the end side, neutral cancel button on the start side, clear consequence text in Arabic ("سيتم إلغاء الحجز ولا يمكن التراجع").
- Toast: announced via aria-live, auto-dismiss after 5 seconds (persistent for errors), maximum 3 visible, includes an icon and an optional "تراجع" (undo) action for reversible operations.

### Loading, empty, and error states

- Use skeleton placeholders that match the final layout (not generic spinners) for pages and lists. Simulate realistic latency of 250 to 600ms in the mock services so skeletons are actually visible and layout shift is verified.
- EmptyState: 32px icon in a light-teal circle, a short title, one-line explanation, and a primary action when one exists (for example "لا توجد حجوزات قادمة" with a "احجز موعد" button).
- ErrorState: clear Arabic message, retry button, and no technical jargon.

