## 32. MICRO-INTERACTIONS, FEEDBACK, AND POLISH

- Every clickable element has a visible hover (desktop), pressed (all devices), and focus-visible state. Cards that are links lift only by border and background change, not by large shadows.
- Buttons that trigger async operations show loading, then success feedback (toast or inline check) and never remain ambiguous.
- Optimistic updates for low-risk actions (mark notification as read, pin a note) with rollback on failure.
- Form submit: disable the submit button while processing, move focus to the first error if invalid, show a success toast and navigate to the logical next page when valid.
- Destructive or irreversible actions always require a ConfirmDialog; reversible ones use a toast with "تراجع".
- Page transitions: a 200ms fade; no sliding page transitions.
- Count-up animations, confetti, and decorative animations are not allowed. The only celebratory moment is the animated check on booking confirmation (a short SVG stroke animation, disabled for reduced motion).
- Long text rules: names truncate with ellipsis in compact cards (with the full name in a title or tooltip), descriptions clamp to 2 lines, and nothing ever overflows its container. Test with very long Arabic names and addresses.
- Skeletons match final layout dimensions so Cumulative Layout Shift stays below 0.1.
- Scroll behavior: restore scroll position on back navigation, scroll to top on new route, and smooth-scroll only for in-page anchors.
- Mobile browser details: use env(safe-area-inset-*) for fixed bars, 100dvh instead of 100vh, input font size at least 16px, -webkit-tap-highlight-color transparent with custom pressed states, overscroll-behavior contain inside drawers and sheets, and touch-action tuned for horizontal scrollers.
- Copy writing: short Arabic sentences, action-oriented button labels ("احجز الآن"، "تأكيد الحجز", never "إرسال" or "OK"), friendly error messages that explain what to do next, consistent terminology across the whole site (one word per concept).

## 33. DATA VISUALIZATION AND DASHBOARD DETAILS

- No chart libraries. Build lightweight SVG components: Sparkline, BarMini, ProgressRing, and a segmented horizontal bar for status distribution.
- KPI card anatomy: icon in a light-teal rounded square at the start, label in secondary text, large tabular number (28 to 32px, weight 700), and an optional trend line with a small arrow and text such as "+12% عن أمس" (green for positive outcomes, red for negative outcomes, always with an arrow icon and text).
- Charts must have text alternatives (aria-label summarizing the data) and a "عرض البيانات" toggle revealing the values in a simple table.
